From: knulli
Subject: [PATCH] video: sunxi: disp2: add the Anbernic H700 panels

disp2 enables the timing controller (and its vblank irq) only from the open
flow of the panel driver named by lcd_driver_name.  The vendor 4.9 tree has
drivers for the Anbernic panels (fog_fj035fhd05_v1, rg34xx_v1, rg34xxsp_v1),
the orangepi one does not, so on 5.4 the LCD stays dark and there are no
vsyncs: everything waiting on a page flip hangs.

One driver serves all three names.  It runs the panel init sequence itself
over the bit-banged 3-wire SPI bus on lcd_gpio_0..4 (vendor reset pulse,
command table, exit sleep, display on), so the display no longer depends on
U-Boot having configured the panel and survives a panel power cycle.  The
tables in anbernic_panels.h are the vendor U-Boot's own sequences
(board/allwinner/h700/panels/*.txt, generated by
board/allwinner/h700/scripts/panel2c.py); the device tree names them with
lcd_panel_init = "<old>", "<boe>" and lcd_id_gpio (PE6, pull-up, low = boe)
tells the two panel generations apart the way the vendor does.

diff -urN base/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/anbernic_panels.h new/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/anbernic_panels.h
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/anbernic_panels.h	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/anbernic_panels.h	2026-09-24 18:24:57.943430619 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,555 @@
